    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d325">

                <pb facs="0445" n="435" sameAs="frus:frus1942China/pg435"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.51/7384: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Gauss</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Chungking</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1942-01-12T11:00:00+07:00">January 12,
                            1942—11 a.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received January 12—6:36 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>33. TF–15. From Fox for the Secretary of the Treasury.</p>
                <p>“Have been requested by Generalissimo and Dr. Kung to return for brief period to
                    report to you on the Chinese internal financial and economic situation. Leaving
                    tomorrow at 24 hours notice.”<anchor n="45" xml:id="d325-f1"/>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Gauss</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d325-f1" n="45" xml:id="d325-f1-content">
                <p>Mr. Fox was delayed three days in leaving Chungking and detained a number of days
                    in India due to air transportation difficulties.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
